                <p>See <ref target="#d159">Documents 159</ref> and <ref target="#d168"
                    >168</ref>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d268-f3" n="2" xml:id="d268-f3-content">
                <p>On July 15 Ledward again called on Steeves
                    to discuss the alleged U.S.-U.K. understanding regarding West New Guinea. He
                    noted that during a June 15 meeting in London between Foreign Secretary
                        Lloyd and Foreign Minister Luns, Luns requested assurances of assistance in the event of a
                    Netherlands-Indonesian armed conflict over West New Guinea. Steeves replied that the U.S. position was the
                    same as that outlined to Ledward in their earlier conversation of July 5: “That
                    we were willing to continue discussions with the UK and Australia but that we could not go any further with the
                    Dutch than Secretary of State Dulles had in 1958.”
                    (Memorandum of conversation by Bell, July
                    15; Department of State, Central Files, 656.98/7–1560)</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
